<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sparta</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Spartan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sparta was a city-state in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, famous for its military society. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mixed-constitution">mixed constitution</a> of kings, council and assembly was admired by ancient writers. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a> mention Sparta in discussing the Carthaginian constitution.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sparta.jpg" alt="Sparta" width="320" height="337" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: T8612 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Spartan_Territory_Before_371_BC.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
